            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Economic Achievements</strong><br>\nUnder Sargon's rule, the Akkadian Empire prospered. He standardized weights and measures, which helped to facilitate trade. The empire's economy was also bolstered by the introduction of the Akkadian language as the lingua franca, making communication across diverse cultures smoother and more efficient.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Relations with the Gods</strong><br>\nReligion played a significant role in Sargon's rule. He claimed to have been chosen by the goddess Inanna, and he used this divine endorsement to justify his rule. Temples and religious practices flourished during his time, and Sargon often participated in religious ceremonies to demonstrate his piety and solidify his relationship with the gods.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Legacy of Sargon</strong><br>\nSargon of Akkad's legacy endured long after his death. He was remembered as a great conqueror and builder who established one of the world's first empires. Future generations of Mesopotamians looked back at his reign as a golden age of power and prosperity. His empire set the stage for the later Babylonian and Assyrian empires to follow in the region.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
